# TutorMunk blog redirect map (groundwork, 14 Aug 2026)
#
# One line per migrated post: old sproutsacademy.com.au URL -> new
# tutormunk.com.au blog URL. Generated from the sourceUrl field in each
# post's markdown frontmatter (src/content/blog/*.md).
#
# IMPORTANT: this file deploys on the SPROUTS ACADEMY domain's server at
# switchover (sproutsacademy.com.au), not on TutorMunk's own
# deploy/.htaccess. It tells the OLD domain where to send visitors who
# still have an old article URL bookmarked or ranked in Google. Whoever
# manages the Sprouts Academy hosting needs this file at that point, it
# does nothing sitting in this repo on its own.
#
# Currently empty of real redirects: the one migrated post
# (selective-test-timeline) has no sourceUrl on file yet, its real old
# Sprouts Academy URL was not supplied, and none has been invented here.
# Add a line below in this format once a post's frontmatter sourceUrl is
# filled in:
#
# https://sproutsacademy.com.au/blog/old-post-slug -> https://tutormunk.com.au/blog/new-post-slug
